<setup>

  <selectFromSequence name="a" from="8" to="12" step="1" />
  <selectFromSequence name="b" from="0.25" to="0.35" step="0.25" />
  <selectFromSequence name="c" from="4" to="6" step="1" />

  <function name="f" symbolic="false">1/(1+$a*e^(-$b*x))</function>
  <function name="g" symbolic="false">1/(1+$a*e^(-$b*x))-$$f(0)</function>
  <derivative name="gP" symbolic="false">$g</derivative>
  <function name="L" symbolic="false" styleNumber="3" labelPosition="lowerRight">$$gP($c)(x-$c) + $$g($c)</function>
    <point name="A" styleNumber="2" coords="($c,$$g($c))" showCoordsWhenDragging="false" draggable="false" labelPosition="lowerRight">
      <label><m>A = $A.coords</m></label>
    </point>
    <point name="B" styleNumber="3" coords="($c+5,$$L($c+5))" showCoordsWhenDragging="false" draggable="false" labelPosition="lowerRight">
      <label><m>B = $B.coords</m></label>
    </point>
    <point name="C" styleNumber="1" coords="($c+5,$$g($c+5))" showCoordsWhenDragging="false" draggable="false" labelPosition="upperLeft">
      <label><m>C = $C.coords</m></label>
    </point>

  <label name="gLabel" anchor="(14,$$g(14)+0.08)"><m>y = s(t)</m></label>
  <label name="LLabel" anchor="(16,$$L(16)-0.09)"><m>y = L(t)</m></label>

</setup>

  <p>Let <m>s</m> be the distance a person has walked along a straight path, in miles, as a function of time <m>t</m> in minutes.  The function <m>s(t)</m> is given by the graph below and <m>L</m> its tangent line at the point <m>A</m>.</p>

<!--  <p><m>a = $a</m>, <m>b = $b</m>, and <m>c = $c</m>, so <m>g(x) = $$g(x)</m> and <m>L(x) = $$L(x)</m>, plus <m>A = $A</m> and <m>B = $B</m></p> -->

    <!-- <figure> -->
      <graph xmin="-1" xmax="21" ymin="min($$g(-1),$$L(-1))-.1" ymax="max($$g(21),$$L(21))+.1" size="medium" fixAxes="true" showNavigation="false" displayXAxis="true" displayYAxis="true" fixed>
        <shortDescription>Graph of a curve and its tangent line at point A, along with a point B on the tangent line and a point C on the curve.</shortDescription>
        <description>Plot of <m>y = g(x)</m> and its tangent line at the point <m>A</m> which has coordinates <m>$A.coords</m>.  Additionally, the point <m>B</m> on <m>y=L(t)</m> with coordinates <m>$B.coords</m> and the point <m>C</m> on <m>y=s(t)</m> with coordinates <m>$C.coords</m> are labeled.</description>
        $g $A $L $B $C $gLabel $LLabel
      </graph>
      <!-- <caption>Plot of <m>y = g(x)</m> and its tangent line at the point <m>A</m></caption>
    </figure> -->

  <p>Use the given information to complete the following sentences. </p>
  <p>At the instant when <m>a = $c</m> minutes, we know that the person has walked<answer><shortDescription>enter distance walked</shortDescription><award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute> $$g($c)
        </award></answer> miles and that their instantaneous velocity at that moment is <answer><shortDescription>enter instaneous velocity</shortDescription><award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute> $$gP($c)
        </award></answer> miles per minute.
  </p>
  <p>
    Between <m>t = $c</m> and <m>t = <math simplify="numbers">$c+5</math></m>, the person walked <answer><shortDescription>enter distance walked</shortDescription><award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute> $$g($c+5)-$$g($c)
          </award></answer> miles, and their average velocity was <answer><shortDescription>enter average velocity</shortDescription><award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute> ($$g($c+5)-$$g($c))/5
          </award></answer> miles per minute.
  </p>
